  "notes": "Cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields since no official cause code was assigned; narrative states 'no specific failure mode of the purge compressor was identified' after troubleshooting ruled out several other causes. Two distinct reportability bases apply: (1) TS-prohibited condition (missed Mode 3 transitions) under 50.73(a)(2)(i)(B), and (2) combined ~9.5 hr period where both CR Chillers were inoperable simultaneously, reportable under 50.73(a)(2)(v) as a condition that could have prevented fulfillment of a safety function. Modeled as two related but distinct Consequence nodes. 122 CR Chiller modeled as a Component (not System) consistent with narrative treatment as the redundant train chiller; SCWS modeled as the governing System. No block_13 data was provided in FORM-366 fields (empty array), so none was fabricated. 'Previous Similar Events' section explicitly states none in past three years, so no stub LER was created per rule 9's requirement of an actual referenced prior event."
